    <string name="permission_autostart_required">Autostart permission must be enabled in settings</string>
    <string name="permission_autostart_help">To ensure the app keeps running in the background and can receive SMS:\n\n• Xiaomi (MIUI): Security app → Autostart management\n• Huawei/Honor: Phone Manager → Protected apps\n• OPPO: Settings → Battery → App autostart\n• Vivo: Settings → More settings → Permission management → Autostart\n• Samsung: Settings → Apps → Auto start\n\nPlease enable autostart for PigeonPost to improve reliability.</string>
    
    <!-- Foreground service special use explanation (Android 14+) -->
    <!--
      Referenced from AndroidManifest.xml via PROPERTY_SPECIAL_USE_FGS_EXPLANATION, so it must NOT
      be translated: resources referenced from the manifest cannot vary by configuration. The system
      Settings app therefore always shows the English text.
    -->
    <string name="fgs_special_use_explanation" translatable="false">PigeonPost runs a foreground service to monitor and forward incoming SMS messages in real-time. This is essential for the core functionality of the app: receiving SMS notifications when you\'re away from your phone and forwarding them to your email. The service must remain active to ensure no messages are missed.</string>
